{
  "subject": {
    "slug": "patient-care",
    "title": "Patient Care",
    "order": 4
  },
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "patient-evaluation-assessment",
    "title": "Patient Evaluation & Assessment",
    "order": 0,
    "pages": [
      {
        "title": "Evaluation and Assessment in RT",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Before and throughout treatment, you're continually gathering information about how a patient is doing \u2014 from the initial history taken at consultation through the side effects you observe on treatment day 20. This isn't diagnosing; it's noticing and reporting accurately."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Subjective vs. Objective Data",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Good history-taking combines two kinds of information:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Subjective data",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " comes from the patient's own report \u2014 their emotions, pain level, or how they describe a symptom. "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Objective data",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " is measurable and observable \u2014 vital signs, visible findings, test results."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Good questioning skills draw out accurate subjective data without leading the patient toward an answer."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page2_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "A patient's respiratory rate of 22 breaths/min is an example of:"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Subjective data",
              "Objective data"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "A measured respiratory rate is objective \u2014 it doesn't rely on the patient's own description."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Cancer Risk Factors and Screening",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Understanding common risk factors (tobacco use, family history, prior radiation exposure, certain infections, occupational exposures) helps you understand why a patient's treatment plan looks the way it does, and supports informed conversations about screening and prevention with patients and their families."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Head and Neck Cancer Side Effects",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Head and neck radiation carries a distinct side-effect profile:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Dysphagia",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 difficulty swallowing"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Mucositis/stomatitis",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 inflamed, radiosensitive mucous membranes that can ulcerate"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Xerostomia",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 dry mouth, raising the risk of dental caries and oral infection"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Taste changes",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Periodontal disease",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 healing after radiation is poor, so extractions afterward risk osteoradionecrosis"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Management includes saliva substitutes for xerostomia, \"magic mouthwash\" for mucositis pain, and early dietitian involvement given how much these effects impact eating."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Pelvic, Breast, and Lung Cancer Side Effects",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Pelvic treatments",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " commonly cause acute GI effects \u2014 diarrhea, abdominal cramping, rectal discomfort \u2014 alongside skin erythema."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Breast treatments",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " typically involve acute skin changes, fatigue, and a risk of lymphedema."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Lung treatments",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " can cause esophagitis (with dysphagia), anorexia, weight loss, and skin changes in the treatment field."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "In every case, the pattern is the same: side effects cluster around the anatomy in the beam path, and management is proactive, not just reactive."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Skin Reaction Staging",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Radiation skin reactions progress in a predictable sequence as dose accumulates:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Faint erythema",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " (~1600 cGy) \u2014 slight redness. Avoid alcohol-based creams, heat/cold/wind/soaps/shaving on the area; wear loose cotton clothing."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Erythema",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " (~2000\u20133000 cGy) \u2014 more pronounced redness, possible itching. Same care, plus hydrocortisone cream if itchy."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Dry desquamation",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " (~3000\u20134000 cGy) \u2014 dry, flaking, peeling skin. May need a prescription cream."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Moist desquamation",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " (~4000\u20136000 cGy) \u2014 seeping, wet skin, sloughing \u2014 most common late in treatment, and the highest infection risk of the four stages."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page6_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "A patient's treatment field shows wet, seeping skin with some sloughing near the end of their course. This best matches:"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Faint erythema",
              "Dry desquamation",
              "Moist desquamation"
            ],
            "answer": 2,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Seeping, wet, sloughing skin late in treatment is characteristic of moist desquamation, the most advanced stage in this progression."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Dietary Counseling by Treatment Site",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Nutrition needs shift by treatment site and by how side effects progress:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Head & neck:",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " maintain weight and hydration; shift toward liquid/pureed diet and protein supplement drinks as swallowing worsens; avoid spicy, coarse, or extreme-temperature foods"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Pelvic:",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " high protein, low residue, high water intake; simple carbohydrates tend to be better tolerated"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Breast:",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " generally a typical diet with high water/protein and produce; avoid alcohol"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Lung:",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " softer foods, high water and protein, liquid diet if swallowing becomes difficult"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Common problems (poor appetite, taste changes, swallowing difficulty) all trace back to identifiable causes tied to the treatment site \u2014 which is why dietary management is site-specific, not one-size-fits-all."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Blood Studies Relevant to RT",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Common labs you'll see referenced in a patient's chart:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "CBC (Complete Blood Count)",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 monitors for treatment-related myelosuppression, especially relevant with concurrent chemotherapy or large-field/marrow-involving treatments"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "BUN/Creatinine/eGFR",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 kidney function, relevant to contrast safety (see Pharmacology & Contrast Media)"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "PSA",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 used in prostate cancer monitoring"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Factors like hydration, medications, and recent illness can all affect these values \u2014 a single abnormal result is a prompt to look closer, not necessarily a crisis."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Wrap-Up",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "You've covered subjective vs. objective data, cancer risk factors, site-specific side effects, the four stages of radiation skin reaction, dietary counseling by site, and relevant blood studies."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Good assessment is about noticing changes early and reporting them accurately \u2014 you're the team member seeing the patient most often, which makes your observations genuinely clinically valuable."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
